Version: [current]
Command: monochange skill install

Write SKILL.md and every bundled reference into a directory the agent runtime reads as a skill. The directory is normally named `monochange` inside the runtime's skills folder. An existing skill is never replaced unless --force is passed.

[1m[97mUsage:[0m [93mmonochange skill install[0m [95m[OPTIONS][0m

[1m[96mOptions:[0m
      [93m--dir[0m[95m [0m[95m<DIR>[0m
          Skill directory to write, for example ~/.claude/skills/monochange

      [93m--force[0m
          Replace an existing skill in the destination

  [93m-h[0m, [93m--help[0m
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

[1m[96mGlobal Options:[0m
  [93m-q[0m, [93m--quiet[0m
          Suppress result, progress, and diagnostic output without changing execution

  [93m-v[0m, [93m--verbose[0m
          Show full result lists and logs, every step timing, and progress notes

      [93m--progress-format[0m[95m [0m[95m<FORMAT>[0m
          Control progress output on stderr

          [possible values: auto, unicode, ascii, json]

      [93m--jq[0m[95m [0m[95m<EXPRESSION>[0m
          Filter explicit JSON output; requires `--format json` or `--format json-min`

      [93m--snapshot[0m
          Print a normalized JSON snapshot for this command subtree
